otal":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.5.dev1.mono.official [97241ffea]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev1.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-3570K CPU @ 3.40GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I opened Quick Open... dialog I got these error messages:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba8857c3-1b0e-40aa-9f7a-b0a8aab04f65)\n\nMy first though was that my project is somehow corrupted. When I searched for these unrecognized UIDs are, I found them from `quick_open_dialog_cache.cfg`. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da022bc1-29dd-4a24-aa87-63ad6aeca75a)\n\nSo the cache contains files I have already deleted. I think this is a quite normal thing to happen with caches. \n\nIn my opinion no error message should be displayed here. This error message only makes the user to suspect that something is broken. Even displaying the source of the error (quick open dialog cache) would be useless because users do not care about this kind of internal editor things.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add new gdscript file to a project\n2. Open the added gdscript file using Quick Open (`Shift-Alt-O` in Windows)\n3. Quit Godot\n4. Delete the added gdscript file manually\n5. Start Godot and load the project\n6. Open Quick Open dialog\n==> `Unrecognized UID`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.gith